  "query_preview": "..\nToday and Sunday: A Low pushing through Central Canada will \nswing a dry cold front through the Pacific Northwest this \nmorning. With very little moisture associated with front, the \nonly area with possible precip chances is along the Cascade \ncrest. The main features with the cold front passage are \nincreasing westerly winds and the colder temperatures. The front\nwill pass during the morning hours. Westerly winds will be \nsustained in the teens to low 20s mph with gusts into the mid \n30s. The best areas for the winds are the upper Basin and \nCascade ridges with 40-70% probability. The speeds not promote \nblowing dust potential but some isolated areas could be \npossible. Winds will wane by the evening hours. Daytime highs \nwill be in the upper 50s to low 70s on Saturday and 50s and low \n60s on Sunday. Overnight lows will be in the upper 20s and 30s \nfor Saturday and 30s and low 40s on Sunday. Overnight patchy \nfrost could impact any remaining gardens and sensitive seasonal \nplants. \n\nMonday through Wednesday: A trough will be digging a low along \nto coast into California. The Low becomes cutoff and a split \nflow pattern develops over the Northwest. It will bring dry, \nwarm pattern over the Inland Northwest. The region can expect \nwarm daytime and cold overnight conditions. Winds will be \ngenerally calm except a brief period of breezy winds down the \nOkanogan Valley on Tuesday with gusts into the upper 20 mph \nrange. Highs will be in the 60s. Overnight lows will be in the \nupper 20s and 30s. Overnight patchy frost could impact any \nremaining gardens and sensitive seasonal plants. \n\nThursday and Friday: The Low finally ejects northeast as a \ntrough moves into the Pacific Northwest. It is bringing \nincreased precip chances but amounts are not expected to more \nthan a couple of hundredths. The probability of any \nprecipitation to occur over the Cascade crest and in the Idaho \nPanhandle is between 30-40%. Snow levels dropping down to around\n5,000 feet Thursday night. Highs will be in the 50s to low 60s.\nOvernight lows will be in the upper 20s and 30s. /JDC",
